			"notes": "# Seed Atlas 0.4.0 — world waypoint labels\n\nMinecraft Java **1.21.11**, Fabric Loader **0.19.5+**, Java **21+**. Replace the previous Seed Atlas JAR and restart Minecraft; keep only one installed.\n\n## Waypoint controls\n\n- Removed the duplicate Waypoint action from the wide Map screen's search sidebar. Map and Search each have one **Waypoint / Clear waypoint** control pair.\n- **Waypoint** uses the selected structure as your destination. **Clear waypoint** removes the destination from the map, minimap, direction HUD and world label, and clears the selected highlight.\n- **Show on map** is now available on the Search tab only. It opens the Map centered on the selected result. It is separate from setting a navigation destination and is disabled until a result is selected.\n- The map footer keeps the selected name/coordinates readable across the full map width. Pointer movement, panning and zoom still retain selection.\n\n## Label visible through terrain\n\n- A floating dark text bar marks the active destination in your world view, with the **structure's item icon, name and horizontal distance in blocks**.\n- Its screen position follows the destination's world position as you move or turn. The label is drawn over the world, so walls, mountains, entities and fog do not hide it.\n- Structure predictions now retain their native generation-point height for the label anchor, including underground structures. Coordinates remain predicted navigation targets rather than exact entrances.\n- Custom right-click waypoints use loaded terrain height when available, otherwise the player's height when the waypoint is set. No extra chunks are loaded.\n- The label appears when the destination is in front of the camera and inside the view. The existing directional HUD helps when the destination is off-screen. F1, open menus and other dimensions hide the label.\n- **Settings → Appearance → World waypoint label** toggles it independently of the directional HUD and minimap. The label uses the structure's item icon even when map symbols are set to letters.\n- Clearing the waypoint, changing world/dimension/seed or disconnecting removes the active label. Waypoints remain session-local; the world/server seed library is unchanged.\n\n## Implementation and status\n\nThe world position uses Minecraft 1.21.11's native waypoint screen projector and ordinary HUD item/text drawing. This avoids custom graphics state or new texture uploads. Existing four-argument Location construction remains available; generated locations additionally retain a nullable Y value.\n\nProduction compilation and JAR/source remapping succeeded with `gradlew.bat assemble --console plain`. No tests were added/run and no Minecraft client was launched. The existing client-check button label was updated to **Show on map**; the check itself was not run. Projection/alignment, through-wall appearance, GUI scales, camera modes, controls and inventory transitions still need in-game confirmation.\n\nThe user reports that 0.3.0 works and looks good."
		},
