			"notes": "# Seed Atlas v0.1.0\n\nFirst release for **Minecraft Java 1.21.11**, **Fabric Loader 0.19.5+**, and **Java 21+**.\n\n## Features\n\n- In-game seed cracking using the adapted SeedCrackerX core. The map becomes available automatically when a seed is recovered.\n- Native biome maps for the Overworld, Nether, and End, with player tracking, pan/zoom, and selectable structure layers.\n- Nearest-structure search around your current player position, with 2,048- and 8,192-block search ranges and live distance ordering.\n- Local waypoints with coordinates, direction, distance, and an optional HUD label.\n- Pause/resume, loaded-chunk rescanning, manual seed entry, and a singleplayer seed shortcut.\n- Explicit local session save/restore with world-hash checks and cleanup when changing connections. No automatic seed uploads or external map service.\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Use a **Fabric 1.21.11** Minecraft instance with **Fabric Loader 0.19.5 or newer**.\n2. Download **`seedatlas-0.1.0-fabric-1.21.11.jar`** from the assets below and put it in that instance's `mods` folder. Fabric API and the seedfinding libraries are bundled.\n3. Start Minecraft and press **M**, or run the client command **`/seedatlas`**. The key can be changed in Controls.\n\n**Remove any separate SeedCrackerX installation before using Seed Atlas.** Both contain the same cracking core.\n\n## Verified\n\nThe build, production remap, and native generation checks passed. An automated Minecraft client run also passed actual loaded-chunk shipwreck detection, seed recovery from 18 generated structure clues, automatic map activation, structure layers, nearest search, waypoints, local save/restore, GUI scaling, and disconnect cleanup.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- Public-server multiplayer has not yet been tested live. The mod is client-side and does not require a server installation.\n- Predictions target vanilla **1.21.11** generation. Custom generation, changed structure salts, spoofed seed hashes, and chunks generated on older versions can cause mismatches or prevent cracking.\n- The map shows a **Y=64 biome slice** and predicted structure start locations. Terrain relief, nearest-biome search, slime chunks, and dungeon/ore maps are not included in this release.\n- Modern **Nether-only seed cracking is unsupported**. Nether and End map predictions are available from a normal recovered world seed.\n- Structure layers cover up to 4,096 blocks around the map view center; nearest search uses its own selected range. Session saving currently has one local slot.\n\n[Usage guide](https://github.com/italixcs/seedatlas/blob/v0.1.0/README.md) · [Validation details](https://github.com/italixcs/seedatlas/blob/v0.1.0/VALIDATION.md) · [Credits and licenses](https://github.com/italixcs/seedatlas/blob/v0.1.0/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)\n\nA `.sha256` file is attached alongside the installable JAR."
